; Probe two cells side by side (copy of #R$A9B4)
;
; The same code as #R$A9B4, used by the crouching branch of #R$A8A5 for the head: the flags of the cells at (x+B, y+C)
; and (x+B+3, y+C) are ORed into E (E starts at 0). Three units are less than the 4 units of a cell, so the two points
; are in the same or in neighbouring cell columns. B is left increased by 3.
; .
; Hardware: none; reads the tile flag map.
;
; HL Position: H = x, L = y (2-pixel units)
; B Offset of the first point in x
; C Offset of the first point in y
; D Column mask (always $1F)
; O:E OR of the tile flags at the points
; O:B B + 3
@label=ProbePair2
c$A96F LD E,$00   ;
 $A971 CALL $A9FE ;
 $A974 INC B      ;
 $A975 INC B      ;
 $A976 INC B      ;
 $A977 JP $A9FE   ;
